 okanagan  territory  and a reminder there is support  available for survivors of residential  schools and their families the number is  toll-free 24 hours a day it's 1-800-721  music from the past in a performance  that seems like it's from the future  swedish super group abba beaming back on  a new digital stage  [Music]  thousands of abba fans are buzzing after  watching the swedish super group perform  some of its biggest hits looking exactly  like it did when they split up 40 years  ago crystal gomezing shows us why this  was no ordinary concert with the band  beaming itself back to life  [Applause]  the music  the makeup  the mood  abba is back  having called on the world to again take  a chance on them abba kicked off a world  first concert going experience in london  absolutely fantastic  if i died tonight i'd die happy  brilliant it was unbelievable it was  extraordinary the arena here in east  london was specially created for abba  voyage it's an immersive experience with  seating around a dance floor huge  screens and a live band and the avatars  unlike this rudimentary likeness we  whipped up were painstakingly created  over years  [Music]  we spent five and a half years in this  and we're all in our 70s i don't think  we'll do another one so no more to come  i think not i'd say i say definitely no  but never say never but it's a no people  have a second life  yeah  the avatars go on living you know  the avatars portray the band members in  their youthful primes the real group  performed over five weeks wearing motion  capture suits at times younger dancers  were brought in to pull off some of the  moves but the result  a concert like no other oh my goodness  it was so good it was like i was beamed  up in a spaceship branded by abba i  danced i jived i had the time of my life  it was like it ticked all the boxes  speaking of boxes much like ikea  furniture abba voyage can be packed and  reassembled anywhere in the world  maybe it's a swedish thing crysta